return {
    ["\n尼尔说这条路他走过七次。\n一路上，他说了三遍。我不信——如果他真的走过七次，为什么连帐篷都不会搭？我蹲在他身后，看他第三次把帐篷布穿反，雪水渗进手套，冷得像在舔我的骨头。\n万幸，我们在天黑前支起了帐篷。\n\n剩余物资：\n面包6份      佩姬给我们准备了18磅，分成了8份\n肉干和肉肠5份\n糖1罐\n黄油4块\n酒3瓶        晚上庆祝，消耗1瓶\n水5瓶        暂时充足，不过路上可以留意水源\n\n\n我想起来，在上山的路上我和尼尔还碰到一个奇怪的人——一个什么装备都没有带，穿着整齐西装的男子，看样子四十来岁，很有气质，眼睛是深蓝色的，很好看。\n我很少会注意一个人的眼睛，但从见到他开始，我就一直盯着他眼睛看，我从他的瞳孔中看到了我的影子。\n他友好地向我们询问下山的路，我指给他我们来时的路。"] = "\nNeil said he has walked this road seven times.\nAlong the way, he said it three times. I don't believe it—if he really had walked it seven times, why couldn't he even set up a tent? I crouched behind him, watching him put the tent fabric on backward for the third time. Snow water seeped into my gloves, cold enough to feel like it was licking my bones.\nFortunately, we set up the tent before dark.\n\nRemaining supplies:\nBread 6 portions      Peggy prepared 18 pounds for us, divided into 8 portions\nBeef jerky and sausages 5 portions\nSugar 1 jar\nButter 4 blocks\nWine 3 bottles        Celebrating tonight, consumed 1 bottle\nWater 5 bottles        Currently sufficient, but we can keep an eye out for water sources on the road\n\n\nI remember, on the way up the mountain, Neil and I met a strange person—a man in a neat suit who didn't carry any equipment. He looked to be in his forties, very charismatic, with deep blue eyes, very beautiful.\nI rarely pay attention to a person's eyes, but from the moment I saw him, I kept staring at his eyes. I saw my own reflection in his pupils.\nHe asked us for the way down the mountain in a friendly manner, and I pointed him to the path we had come from.",
